Why I had the spellbooks at hand is, of course, a good question, and
one of the lessons I learned from this game (which ended sadly when I
was overcome by Wizard-summoned nasties *after* I had killed the Wizard
the first time).  My first thought was wanting them handy when I did
need them (and once I had a bag of holding, they weren't so bad
weight-wise), but with the Eye (and thus easy level-teleport), that's
pretty much a non-issue.

(Irrelevant to this thread, but:  Lesson #2: blessed-genocide L when
you have the chance; krakens (my first non-blessed genocide, from a
throne) are good to get rid of, but arch-liches are just nasty.  Lesson
#3: finger of death is a very useful spell, so as a wizard, especially
post-Quest when you have gobs of power regen, getting crowned isn't so
bad.)



